@startuml d-02-token-options
' Decision D-02 (SRC-Q "Token management"): how does a TPP request reach the ASPSP gateway
' with PSU authority? PROPOSAL generated by AI on 2026-09-19. Options only — not a decision.
' Note: under the Berlin Group standard a bearer token exists only if OAuth2 is used as a
' pre-step or as the OAuth2 SCA approach (SRC-IG §4.3). With plain redirect SCA the TPP presents
' the Consent-ID header and is bound by its QWAC, and there may be no TPP token at all (D-03).
title D-02 — options for carrying TPP/PSU authority from Finologee to the ASPSP gateway

participant "TPP" as TPP
participant "Finologee" as FIN
participant "Ping Federate" as PING
participant "ASPSP gateway" as GW

== Option A — pass-through: gateway accepts the Finologee-issued token ==
TPP -> FIN : API call + Finologee access token
FIN -> GW : forward call + same token
GW -> FIN : validate token (introspection / JWKS — capability unverified)
note right of GW
  + one issuer, fewest hops
  - bank APIs trust a vendor-issued token;
    revocation and audit depend on Finologee
  - ties the resource model to the vendor's token claims
end note

== Option B — exchange: Finologee token swapped for a bank token at Ping ==
TPP -> FIN : API call + Finologee access token
FIN -> PING : token exchange (e.g. RFC 8693 — support unverified)
PING --> FIN : bank token (audience = ASPSP gateway)
FIN -> GW : forward call + bank token
note right of GW
  + bank APIs accept only bank-issued tokens (SRC-Q: Ping is
    "access token issuer inside the bank")
  + one internal trust model for app and XS2A traffic
  - extra hop and latency; Ping must map TPP + consent claims
end note

== Option C — no token inside: mTLS between Finologee and gateway + signed request context ==
TPP -> FIN : API call (+ Consent-ID, or token terminated at Finologee)
FIN -> GW : forward over mTLS with signed TPP-context header\n(organizationIdentifier, roles, consentId)
note right of GW
  + works whether or not OAuth is used (D-03)
  + gateway authorises from its own consent store (D-01 option A)
  - custom context contract to agree with Finologee (Q-04)
end note
@enduml
